      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The majority's reasoning was fundamentally rooted in the textualist interpretation of the Fourteenth Amendment, which they argued did not confer a substantive right to abortion. The dissent's arguments failed because they relied on an expansive, unenumerated right theory that the majority deemed an overreach beyond the explicit language of the Constitution. Their interpretation essentially sought to create a right where the text provided none, making their legal foundation inherently unsound.",
      "source": "target",
